{"id": "EUVD-2026-71312", "enisaUuid": "9f6d40a6-b014-3702-a2bd-d355d54a46aa", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-tcp: fix usage of page_frag_cache\n\nnvme uses page_frag_cache to preallocate PDU for each preallocated request\nof block device. Block devices are created in parallel threads,\nconsequently page_frag_cache is used in not thread-safe manner.\nThat leads to incorrect refcounting of backstore pages and premature free.\n\nThat can be catched by !sendpage_ok inside network stack:\n\nWARNING: CPU: 7 PID: 467 at ../net/core/skbuff.c:6931 skb_splice_from_iter+0xfa/0x310.\n\ttcp_sendmsg_locked+0x782/0xce0\n\ttcp_sendmsg+0x27/0x40\n\tsock_sendmsg+0x8b/0xa0\n\tnvme_tcp_try_send_cmd_pdu+0x149/0x2a0\nThen random panic may occur.\n\nFix that by serializing the usage of page_frag_cache.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:55:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d19f98c79f1b7e09e4cdf5c20d626e571e487467", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64561afb42d8390695bf810d9bbd087cbca00291", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a9750263ffacbbd2048a391fd4bd22e2146c57d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e4cf281558709b92ec2ca3054fe2ffc69266ef9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36ac05f7cfd59d90c597071304b14e98090d5dd1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r23c-4v3q-555g", "CVE-2026-80862"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bb5e074-c8b0-3745-980b-d7bc42133b3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4e893ca8117022de68ce1b61c0309e3d17bb8a25 <36ac05f7cfd59d90c597071304b14e98090d5dd1"}, {"id": "228c0a04-507b-3ee8-a934-0badb0243989", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4e893ca8117022de68ce1b61c0309e3d17bb8a25 <64561afb42d8390695bf810d9bbd087cbca00291"}, {"id": "4aa46f36-7aa7-3e1f-9a13-1ac9782a0c95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "5e0a2011-6f1f-30bd-9732-03413a393a59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.108"}, {"id": "739714e5-dc19-3826-aa4a-22ef5058004e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "74eec2bd-ab96-3ad3-a4ec-3544c2ef991d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4e893ca8117022de68ce1b61c0309e3d17bb8a25 <6e4cf281558709b92ec2ca3054fe2ffc69266ef9"}, {"id": "760047d9-c88a-38b2-ba2d-751e02d651af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4e893ca8117022de68ce1b61c0309e3d17bb8a25 <0a9750263ffacbbd2048a391fd4bd22e2146c57d"}, {"id": "7aaa8c2a-1709-35f9-a2c7-f1678eba57df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c57506918b078ecab7dedebef0f34dbc23ae2e46"}, {"id": "949f2ce5-d98e-345b-8142-7830463e53a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9f46e384-1ba3-3e9d-889a-1355f2037c71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "cebdad1b-6020-3036-9645-98a70d18681a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "ed63064e-4f7d-39b0-983b-086812f970a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ef5c431e-f5fa-35a7-9f57-6fbc3d50ddd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4e893ca8117022de68ce1b61c0309e3d17bb8a25 <d19f98c79f1b7e09e4cdf5c20d626e571e487467"}, {"id": "fc323aa8-4b5d-35c3-892b-b49f820faf3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.160 <6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7e5ead52-d0d6-3664-8e70-9f3f7c463af5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}